y.ts#getModelContextWindow]] consults [[src/main/config.ts#getModelContextLengthOverride]]. For SSH and Remote connections, the IPC route reads the active model config from that connection and [[src/main/model-context.ts#resolveActiveModelContextWindow]] applies its override only when the requested model still matches, so a delayed response cannot leak the previous model's context window. Missing or invalid overrides fall through to the existing `/models` lookup and finally the renderer heuristic. DeepSeek V4 identifiers have a 1M static fallback; older DeepSeek aliases retain their 128K fallback.","startLine":21,"endLine":21,"text":"For local connections, src/main/model-discovery.ts#getModelContextWindow consults src/main/config.ts#getModelContextLengthOverride. For SSH and Remote connections, the IPC route reads the active model config from that connection and src/main/model-context.ts#resolveActiveModelContextWindow applies its override only when the requested model still matches, so a delayed response cannot leak the previous model's context window. Missing or invalid overrides fall through to the existing /models lookup and finally the renderer heuristic. DeepSeek V4 identifiers have a 1M static fallback; older DeepSeek aliases retain their 128K fallback."},{"markdown":"An explicit `default` query reads both the root model library and root config, even when the Dashboard process runs from a named profile. Omitted or `current` queries retain that process's profile.","startLine":25,"endLine":25,"text":"An explicit default query reads both the root model library and root config, even when the Dashboard process runs from a named profile. Omitted or current queries retain that process's profile."},{"markdown":"The compatibility handler uses upstream's context-local Hermes home override for every explicit profile, including `default`, and resets it after successful or failed config reads. [[tests/hermes-agent-compat-profiles.test.ts]] executes the injected handlers with separate root and named-profile files to verify matching library/config scope, endpoint-aware writes, and recovery after a read failure.","startLine":27,"endLine":27,"text":"The compatibility handler uses upstream's context-local Hermes home override for every explicit profile, including default, and resets it after successful or failed config reads. tests/hermes-agent-compat-profiles.test.ts executes the injected handlers with separate root and named-profile files to verify matching library/config scope, endpoint-aware writes, and recovery after a read failure."},{"markdown":"The gauge's numerator resolves as: exact payload counts (`context_used`, else prompt tokens) → a chars/4 transcript estimate → the previous turn's value. Without the estimate the gauge went blank on providers that return no usage at all (#789).","startLine":31,"endLine":31,"text":"The gauge's numerator resolves as: exact payload counts (context_used, else prompt tokens) → a chars/4 transcript estimate → the previous turn's value. Without the estimate the gauge went blank on providers that return no usage at all (#789)."},{"markdown":"The gauge only renders when `contextTokens` is set (see `contextUsage` in [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/Chat.tsx]]), so on `message.complete` the transport fills it in even when `usageFromPayload` returns null. [[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.ts#estimateContextTokens]] sums the transcript's characters — bubbles, reasoning text, tool call args, and tool results all occupied the prompt loop — and excludes the just-completed assistant reply bubble, because `contextTokens` means prompt-side occupancy and the reply was generated output. The estimate is a floor: system prompt, tool schemas, and attachments aren't visible to the renderer.","startLine":33,"endLine":33,"text":"The gauge only renders when contextTokens is set (see contextUsage in src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/Chat.tsx), so on message.complete the transport fills it in even when usageFromPayload returns null. src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/hooks/useDashboardChatTransport.ts#estimateContextTokens sums the transcript's characters — bubbles, reasoning text, tool call args, and tool results all occupied the prompt loop — and excludes the just-completed assistant reply bubble, because contextTokens means prompt-side occupancy and the reply was generated output. The estimate is a floor: system prompt, tool schemas, and attachments aren't visible to the renderer."},{"markdown":"A failed turn with no usage record does not fabricate an estimate — nothing new entered the context, and the previous gauge value stays.","startLine":35,"endLine":35,"text":"A failed turn with no usage record does not fabricate an estimate — nothing new entered the context, and the previous gauge value stays."},{"markdown":"The bottom status bar shows the visible chat's context fill and token totals, scoped to its connection, profile and conversation. See [[src/renderer/src/screens/Layout/sessionUsage.ts#formatSessionUsage]].","startLine":39,"endLine":39,"text":"The bottom status bar shows the visible chat's context fill and token totals, scoped to its connection, profile and conversation. See src/renderer/src/screens/Layout/sessionUsage.ts#formatSessionUsage."},{"markdown":"[[src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/Chat.tsx]] reports usage upward per run (like loading and title), the shell keeps it on the run, and the bar shows it only on the chat tab. The chip turns to a warning at 80% of the window, using the unrounded ratio.","startLine":41,"endLine":41,"text":"src/renderer/src/screens/Chat/Chat.tsx reports usage upward per run (like loading and title), the shell keeps it on the run, and the bar shows it only on the chat tab. The chip turns to a warning at 80% of the window, using the unrounded ratio."},{"markdown":"An idle session-row read captures its live counter baseline at admission. Starting or completing a turn invalidates pending reads; a late response cannot prove which turn the row included.","startLine":45,"endLine":45,"text":"An idle session-row read captures its live counter baseline at admission. Starting or completing a turn invalidates pending reads; a late response cannot prove which turn the row included."},{"markdown":"The last confirmed row remains available while the next turn runs or metadata is unavailable. [[src/renderer/src/screens/Layout/sessionUsage.ts#combineUsageTotals]] adds only subsequent live gains. A connection/profile/config revision excludes both old live counters and saved metadata immediately. The status bar reads model, mode and skill metadata through a captured profile-editor target, rejecting superseded poll replies. A retained tab on a nonselected connection keeps its totals but omits unavailable connection metadata; it cannot claim the selected machine's state or imply an unknown gateway is offline.","startLine":47,"endLine":47,"text":"The last confirmed row remains available while the next turn runs or metadata is unavailable. src/renderer/src/screens/Layout/sessionUsage.ts#combineUsageTotals adds only subsequent live gains. A connection/profile/config revision excludes both old live counters and saved metadata immediately. The status bar reads model, mode and skill metadata through a captured profile-editor target, rejecting superseded poll replies. A retained tab on a nonselected connection keeps its totals but omits unavailable connection metadata; it cannot claim the selected machine's state or imply an unknown gateway is offline."},{"markdown":"Metadata requires the requested profile's own row. A missing row clears earlier metadata without falling back to another active profile or discarding the visible conversation's token totals.","startLine":49,"endLine":49,"text":"Metadata requires the requested profile's own row. A missing row clears earlier metadata without falling back to another active profile or discarding the visible conversation's token totals."},{"markdown":"Each captured 